{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Quench and temper of 42CrMo4 shafts (template)",
  "notes": "Template for a hardening and tempering study on Ø40 mm 42CrMo4 shafts in a sealed-quench furnace. Factors and responses are defined; no design is applied yet. The quench bath temperature drifts with the load sequence and is recorded as an environmental factor. Suggested start: an optimal (I) design for a quadratic model with about 24 runs, or a response-surface design after a screening round. Hardness is measured at mid-radius (HRC, mean of five indents), impact energy with Charpy V specimens at -20 °C (mean of three), distortion as total runout between centres.",
